MonkMode
========

MonkMode is a tamper-resistant website/app self-control blocker for Windows.
It is a personal fork of the open-source Cold Turkey blocker (GPLv3), rebranded
and being hardened so that a block, once started, cannot be casually removed
before its timer expires. MonkMode is a command-line tool (no GUI).

Project layout
--------------
  /MonkMode       <-- CLI (monkmode.exe): parses commands, writes the hosts file,
                       installs/starts the service, registers the notifier
  /MonkMode_srv   <-- LocalSystem Windows service "MONKMODE": locks the hosts file,
                       kills blocked processes, lifts the block when time is up
  /MM_notify      <-- User-session notifier (mm_notify.exe): kills blocked apps in
                       the user session, compensates for clock changes, and shows a
                       tray-balloon toast when the block ends

See ARCHITECTURE.md for the full component map and the bypass surface.

Usage
-----
  monkmode block --sites reddit.com,youtube.com --for 2h30m
  monkmode block --sites pornhub.com --apps chrome.exe --until "2026-06-11 18:00"
  monkmode block --file blocklist.txt --for 8h
  monkmode status
  monkmode add --sites x.com          (add sites to an active block)
  monkmode help

  --for accepts 45 (minutes), 90m, 2h, 1d12h.  Once a block starts it cannot be
  shortened or replaced until it expires; 'add' can only add more sites.

Building & running
------------------
- Target framework: .NET 8 (net8.0-windows), VB.NET, SDK-style projects.
- Build everything: open MonkMode.sln in Visual Studio 2022, or:
      dotnet build MonkMode.sln -c Release
- Assemble a runnable folder (all three exes must live together, alongside
  monkmode_settings.ini created at block time):
      powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\build-dist.ps1
  Then, from an elevated prompt:
      dist\monkmode.exe block --sites reddit.com --for 2h
- monkmode.exe requests Administrator elevation (it edits the hosts file and
  installs/starts the service via the Service Control Manager; see
  MonkMode/ServiceTools.vb). Requires the .NET 8 desktop runtime.

Migration note
--------------
Originally VB.NET 2010 / .NET Framework 2.0 with a WinForms GUI. Now:
- Migrated all projects to SDK-style .NET 8 (net8.0-windows).
- Replaced the WinForms GUI with a console CLI (Program/Blocker/Crypto).
- Authored MonkMode/ServiceTools.vb (advapi32 P/Invoke) to replace the
  third-party "ServiceTools" helper the original referenced but never shipped.
- Replaced the popup window with a tray-balloon toast in the notifier; dropped
  the MM_notify2 watcher twin and MM_popup window. (A proper restart-watchdog is
  a Phase 3 item.)
- Dropped the unused PowerPacks reference and the dead installutil installer.

Removing the service (development only)
---------------------------------------
  Run as Administrator:  sc delete MONKMODE

  NOTE: this removal path is exactly the kind of bypass the hardening work
  (Phase 3) is meant to close. Documented only because it's needed in dev.

